 {'id':'contact-management','level':'Intermediate','title':'Contact management application','objective':'Store, search, update and delete contact details.','requirements':'Python and JSON or SQLite.','concepts':'Dictionaries, string normalization, CRUD and persistence.','steps':['Define contact fields.','Normalize phone and email input.','Implement create, search, update and delete.','Avoid duplicate contacts.','Save and reload contacts.'],'code':"contacts = {'ava@example.com': {'name': 'Ava', 'phone': '9000000000'}}\nemail = 'ava@example.com'.lower().strip()\nprint(contacts.get(email, 'Not found'))",'output':"{'name': 'Ava', 'phone': '9000000000'}",'explanation':'A normalized email can act as a lookup key. Add stronger validation and database persistence for real use.'},
