 {'id':'ecommerce-backend','level':'Advanced','title':'E-commerce backend','objective':'Model products, carts, orders and checkout workflows.','requirements':'Django or FastAPI, SQL database and payment provider sandbox.','concepts':'OOP, relational modeling, transactions, APIs, authentication and security.','steps':['Model products, inventory, users, carts and orders.','Build catalog and cart endpoints.','Validate stock during checkout in a transaction.','Integrate a payment provider sandbox securely.','Test order state transitions and idempotency.'],'code':"def reserve_stock(available, requested):\n    if requested <= 0: raise ValueError('Quantity must be positive')\n    if requested > available: raise ValueError('Insufficient stock')\n    return available - requested\nprint(reserve_stock(10, 3))",'output':'7','explanation':'This function captures a stock invariant. A real checkout must enforce it atomically in the database to avoid overselling.'},
